    "desc": "Are you someone who brings clarity when there’s a lot moving at once?\n\nAs a Senior Producer, you’ll own the execution picture across shifting priorities, cross-team dependencies, and decisions that can’t wait for every detail to be known. You’ll keep Top Goal teams focused on what they’re trying to achieve, with ownership of delivery outcomes rather than a predefined process.\n\nTHE DIFFERENCE YOU’LL MAKE:\n\nThis is not a coordination-only role. You’ll make complex delivery more predictable by maintaining a clear view of what’s happening, what’s at risk, and what needs a decision. When priorities or circumstances change, you’ll make sure the plan changes with them instead of quietly becoming outdated. That means fewer late surprises and a team that can keep moving without depending on one person to hold the full picture.\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO:\n\n• Lead complex cross-functional initiatives end to end, from early planning through development, launch, and post-launch.\n• Turn product goals into clear, realistic delivery plans, with defined scope, estimates, dependencies, milestones, and quality expectations.\n• Keep delivery on track and transparent by maintaining a clear view of progress, risks, dependencies, and changes, and raising issues early.\n• Drive decisions when plans change - assess trade-offs, bring recommendations, make decisions within your scope, and follow through.\n• Improve how the team delivers by adapting your approach, building ownership within the team, and addressing recurring delivery problems.\n\nWHO YOU’LL WORK WITH:\n\n• You will work closely with a cross-functional Top Goal team spanning Product Management, Game Design, UX/UI, Art, Engineering, QA, Data Science, and Business Analytics.\n• Depending on the initiative, you will also work with other Producers, discipline leads, the Game Lead, central technology teams, marketing, and external partners.\n\nWE ARE A MATCH IF YOU:\n\n• Have 5+ years of experience leading complex product or game development projects across creative and technical disciplines, with ownership of delivery outcomes\n• Have led projects end to end and can show how you handled risks, changing priorities, and things that did not go to plan\n• Can turn incomplete or complex information into a clear, realistic plan while keeping sight of the bigger picture\n• Communicate risks and problems early, separate facts from assumptions, and come to discussions with a recommendation or proposed next step\n• Know how to create the right level of structure and ownership for a team, and can point to feedback that materially changed how you work\n\nBONUS POINTS:\n\n• Experience developing and operating live mobile games, including event calendars and incident handling\n• Experience mentoring other Producers\n• Passion for football and an understanding of football audiences and products\n\nWHY YOU’LL LOVE WORKING HERE:\n\n• The team behind the game: transparency and trust from day one, paired with a strong sense of teamwork- that's the essence of who we are. It's not just what you do - it’s how you do it and who you do it with. With 280+ teammates from around the world, we’re on a mission to bring the joy of winning to millions.\n• We make your life at Nordeus hassle-free: enjoy Nordeus provided breakfast, lunch, snacks, and beverages, a fully-equipped gym, organized sports activities (yoga, Brazilian jiu-jitsu, basketball, football), an ergonomic workstation, top-notch tech equipment (including laptop, mobile phone and bill coverage, and other tech), a kids’ playroom, a music corner, board and video games + latest consoles.\n• Perks? We’ve got plenty: premium private medical insurance for you and your family, flexible working hours, take-what-you-need vacation policy, offsites abroad for the whole company, fully-paid maternity and paternity leave, employee stock purchase plan, access to L&D platforms and opportunities and many more.\n• Make your mark on games played by millions: with over 300M registered users, Top Eleven is the world’s most successful football management game. Golf Rival, with more than 60M registered users, is the #2 mobile golf game, aiming to claim the top spot. With one more game in the works, we are continuing our efforts to create powerful mobile sports gaming experiences built to last.\n• Meaningful career experience: work with experienced game makers and mentors who will support you from day one, helping you map a career path that's true to you.\n• Impact beyond the screen: It is not just about us. We are part of something bigger than a job. We create a better future for generations to come through the efforts of the Nordeus Foundation.\n\nGOOD TO KNOW:\n\n• This is a hybrid, on-site position based in Belgrade.",
