    "desc": "Job Overview\n\nWe are looking for a Middle Frontend Developer to join the Global Content team and work on interactive web projects and portal game mechanics for World of Warships.\n\nYou will be involved in developing and supporting the multilingual and multi-regional World of Warships portal: event pages, web adventures, interactive mechanics, mini-games, visual-heavy interfaces, and portal modules that support in-game events and the overall ecosystem of the project.\n\nThis is a hybrid role at the intersection of interactive frontend development, CMS-driven solutions, and production web development. A large part of the current production codebase is built with vanilla JavaScript, so a strong understanding of native frontend development and browser APIs is important for this role. At the same time, you will participate in expanding Vue 3 usage as a foundation for new solutions and the potential migration of existing projects.\n\nWe are looking for a developer who enjoys building non-standard interactive web mechanics, working with animations and complex frontend behavior, while maintaining stability, performance, and production quality.\n\nWhat will you do?\n\n• Develop and maintain event pages, web adventures, game web mechanics, mini-games, widgets, and portal/web modules\n• Develop frontend solutions using Vue 3, TypeScript, and related tooling\n• Work with production code written in vanilla JavaScript\n• Work with REST APIs, JSON configurations, and data-driven interfaces\n• Implement complex animations and interactive behavior\n• Work with visual-heavy and interactive web interfaces\n• Prepare and maintain frontend bundles for CMS integration\n• Optimize performance of animation-heavy and mobile-heavy pages: asset loading, rendering, lazy loading, browser behavior, and frontend performance\n• Ensure proper functionality across different devices, browsers, regional versions, and language configurations\n• Collaborate with designers using Figma, verify implementations, and prepare/export assets when needed\n• Support and improve reusable components, UI patterns, and shared frontend approaches\n• Write technical documentation and implementation guidelines\n\nWhat are we looking for?\n\n• 3+ years of commercial frontend development experience with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript\n• Strong knowledge of JavaScript (ES6+) and browser APIs\n• Strong HTML5, CSS3, and SCSS skills\n• 2+ years of practical experience with Vue 3\n• Experience with TypeScript and Composition API\n• Experience with mobile web development\n• Strong practical understanding of cross-browser compatibility and platform/browser quirks\n• Experience working with REST APIs, JSON, and asynchronous client-server interactions\n• Experience implementing complex animations and interactive interfaces\n• Experience working with CMS or content-driven web projects\n• Independence in solving technical tasks and finding solutions\n• Attention to implementation quality, interface details, and user experience\n• Ability to work across different types of tasks and contexts\n• Ability to work with existing codebases, refactor code, and maintain production quality\n• Confident use of Figma\n• English sufficient for technical communication and documentation\n\nWhat additional skills will help you stand out?\n\n• Good sense of visual design, composition, and understanding of UI/UX principles for interactive web interfaces (previous design experience would be a plus)\n• Experience with Three.js, WebGL, or other 3D/web graphics solutions\n• Experience with GSAP, ScrollTrigger, and similar solutions\n• Experience with Pinia and Vite\n• Experience working with web analytics or tracking systems\n• Experience with Node.js in the context of frontend tooling, scripts, and build systems\n• Experience working with design systems or custom UI kits\n• Understanding of frontend performance optimization and browser rendering\n• Understanding of frontend bundles and build/deploy flows for CMS integration\n• Basic understanding of frontend delivery pipelines: Nginx, CDN, Object Storage, GitLab CI/CD\n• Basic Photoshop skills\n• Experience working on multilingual and multi-regional projects\n• Russian language skills\n• Links to relevant projects: interactive pages, mini-games, animation-heavy, or 3D/web-heavy cases\n\nWork mode\n\n• Onsite during probation period and hybrid after probation period (3 days of work from the office and 2 days of work form home).\n\nBenefits\n\nBenefits and perks are tailored to the local market and culture. Our benefits in Belgrade include:\n\n• Additional vacation days based on years of service at Wargaming: up to 5 days on top of the statutory minimum\n• Additional paid time off (5 Personal Days, Birthday Leave, Marriage Leave, Compassionate Leave)\n• Sick Leave Compensation, Maternity Leave Benefits\n• Premium Private Health Insurance\n• Career development and education opportunities within the company\n• English clubs and platform for learning languages\n• Mental well-being program (iFeel)\n• Commuting allowance\n• Company events\n• FitPass membership\n• Discounts for employees\n• Personal Gaming Account\n• Coffee, fruits, and snacks in the office\n• On-site canteen with subsidized prices for food and drinks\n• Seniority Awards\n• Referral program - you can recommend the best talents to the Company and receive a reward\n\nPlease submit your CV in English to ensure smooth processing and review.\n\nAbout Wargaming\n\nWargaming is an award-winning online game developer and publisher headquartered in Nicosia, Cyprus. Operating since 1998, Wargaming has become one of the leaders in the gaming industry with 15 offices worldwide, including studios in Chicago, Prague, Shanghai, Tokyo, and Vilnius. Our diverse and multicultural team works together to deliver a top-class experience to millions of players who enjoy Wargaming's titles across all major gaming platforms. Our flagship products include free-to-play hits World of Tanks, World of Warships and World of Tanks Blitz.…",
