    "url": "https://epicgames.com/careers/jobs/6003199004?gh_jid=6003199004",
    "desc": "WHAT MAKES US EPIC?\n\nAt the core of Epic’s success are talented, passionate people. Epic prides itself on creating a collaborative, welcoming, and creative environment. Whether it’s building award-winning games or crafting engine technology that enables others to make visually stunning interactive experiences, we’re always innovating.\n\nBeing Epic means being a part of a team that continually strives to do right by our community and users. We’re constantly innovating to raise the bar of engine and game development.\n\nPRODUCT MANAGEMENT - UNREAL ENGINE\n\nWhat We Do\n\nUnreal-powered projects have led the way in real-time entertainment for over 20 years. Our team of industry experts continuously innovates to enhance the tools and technology that empower developers around the world.\n\nWhat You'll Do\n\nThe Unreal Ecosystem empowers developers to create and publish the next generation of digital entertainment to hundreds of millions of global consumers. As a Senior Director of Product Management, Unreal Ecosystem, you will serve as the senior business partner to our engine development leadership, owning strategy and growth for Unreal Editor for Fortnite, UE6 and other Epic developer tools and services. You will define \\vision and strategy, partner with product development to bring that vision to life, and work closely with our GTM teams to drive adoption and commercial outcomes.You will bring both strategic vision and operational rigor to one of the most consequential platforms in real-time 3D creation and digital entertainment.\n\nIn this role, you will\n\n• Drive ecosystem strategy for Unreal Editor for Fortnite and Unreal Engine, partnering closely with engineering and product leadership to prioritize initiatives that drive creator growth, developer adoption, platform performance, and commercial outcomes\n• Define measurable goals for major roadmap initiatives, track business impact across releases, and use those insights to continuously refine prioritization\n• Stay deeply connected to the UEFN creator and UE developer community, translating their needs and behaviors into ecosystem strategy alongside the creator success team\n• Champion adoption of platform-level social and discovery features, including friends, parties, and text chat into a native layer of the Epic ecosystem\n• Define and grow pathways for developers to participate in the broader epic ecosystem and metaverse economy, shaping new commercial models and open standards\n• Lead and grow a team of product managers, providing mentorship, organizational clarity, and the structure needed to execute a complex, multi-workstream roadmap effectively\n• Collaborate across Product, Engineering, Design, Marketing, and cross-functional partners to align on priorities, requirements, and go-to-market execution for major platform releases\n\nWhat we're looking for\n\n• 12+ years of product management experience, with meaningful time spent on developer tools, game engines, or complex platform ecosystems\n• Deep understanding of the game development process and the needs of creators and developers building on real-time 3D platforms\n• Proven ability to function as a business partner to engineering leadership someone who can bring goal-setting, prioritization frameworks, and growth thinking to a team that builds the platform others build on\n• Experience defining and tracking product KPIs, measuring roadmap impact, and using data to drive decisions\n• Strong understanding of platform ecosystem dynamics such as social features, marketplace integrations, developer services, and how they compound into long-term growth\n• Exceptional communication skills with the ability to align diverse stakeholders, write clear product requirements, and present strategy to senior leadership\n• Experience managing and developing high-performing product managers across multiple concurrent workstreams\n• A genuine passion for the creator and developer community; someone who stays close to how developers and players are evolving and can translate that into a compelling product vision\n\nEPIC JOB + EPIC BENEFITS = EPIC LIFE\n\nOur intent is to cover all things that are medically necessary and improve the quality of life. We pay 100% of the premiums for both you and your dependents. Our coverage includes Medical, Dental, a Vision HRA, Long Term Disability, Life Insurance & a 401k with competitive match. We also offer a robust mental well-being program through Modern Health, which provides free therapy and coaching for employees & dependents. Throughout the year we celebrate our employees with events and company-wide paid breaks. We offer unlimited PTO and sick time and recognize individuals for 7 years of employment with a paid sabbatical.\nABOUT US\n\nEpic Games​ ​is a leading interactive entertainment company. For over 30 years we've been making award-winning games and engine technology that empowers others to make visually stunning games and 3D content that bring environments to life like never before. Epic's award-winning Unreal Engine technology not only provides game developers the ability to build high-fidelity, interactive experiences for PC, console, mobile, and VR, it is also a tool being embraced by content creators across a variety of industries such as media and entertainment, automotive, and architectural design. As we continue to build our Engine technology and develop remarkable games, we strive to build teams of world-class talent.\n\nLike what you hear? Come be a part of something Epic!\n\nEpic Games deeply values diverse teams and an inclusive work culture, and we are proud to be an Equal Opportunity employer. Learn more about our Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Policy here.…",
