    "desc": "ABOUT VOODOO\n\nFounded in 2013, Voodoo is a tech company that creates mobile games and apps with a mission to entertain the world. Gathering 800 employees, 7 billion downloads, and over 200 million active users, Voodoo is the #3 mobile publisher worldwide in terms of downloads after Google and Meta. Our portfolio includes chart-topping games like Mob Control and Paper.io 2, alongside popular apps such as BeReal and Wizz. \n\nThis position is Istanbul-based.\n\n\n\n\nTEAM\n\nYou will be an integral part of a newly established internal studio, a dynamic and focused team dedicated to one of our most promising Puzzle game in scale. This studio is specifically chartered to improve this high-potential game up to the successful and market-ready title it is meant to become. \n\n\n\n\nROLE\n\nAs a Product Manager for one of our Puzzle Studio, you will be at the heart of the game's evolution. You will work closely with a multidisciplinary team of engineers, artists, and product experts to design, test, and refine features that keep our players engaged and entertained.\n\n - Participate in the design and creation of engaging, challenging, and fun levels that maintain player interest and progression\n\n - Develop and iterate on game mechanics and features that enhance the core gameplay loop\n\n - Analyze player behavior, game metrics, and feedback to identify opportunities for improvement\n\n - Collaborate with engineers and artists to bring level designs and features to life\n\n - Structure, run, and monitor A/B tests to validate design decisions and optimize player experience\n\n - Balance game difficulty curves to ensure appropriate challenge and retention across all levels\n\n - Stay up-to-date with the hybrid-casual and puzzle game market, analyzing competitor games and emerging trends\n\n - Test and playtest levels and features to ensure quality and enjoyment\n\n - Contribute to the product roadmap and strategic direction\n\n - Work iteratively, rapidly prototyping ideas and incorporating feedback from the team and data\n   \n   \n\n\nPROFILE\n\n - 2+ years of professional experience in game design, product specialist, or similar role in the mobile gaming industry\n\n - Strong passion for mobile puzzle and hybrid-casual games, with a deep understanding of what makes them engaging and successful\n\n - Analytical mindset with the ability to interpret data, identify trends, and make data-driven design decisions\n\n - Understanding of player psychology and what drives engagement, retention, and satisfaction in puzzle games\n\n - Strong communication skills and ability to clearly articulate design ideas to cross-functional teams\n\n - Iterative mindset with the ability to rapidly test, learn, and improve designs based on feedback\n\n - Fluent in English\n\n - Bonus: Experience with Unity or game development tools, knowledge of A/B testing methodologies, experience shipping successful mobile games\n   \n   \n\n\nBENEFITS: \n\n - Best in Class compensation\n\n - Other benefits according to the country you reside.",
