    "desc": "Blackbird Interactive is a creative-fueled, future-driven, independent game studio where the best talent in the industry can find long-term careers to help grow their abilities while working on a wide range of projects, which encompass world-class IPs as well as our own creations across multiple genres.\n\nOur studio operates as a remote-first workplace, offering flexible work arrangements.\n\nPLEASE NOTE: At this time, we are only able to hire candidates who are legally eligible to work in Canada and reside within Canada.\n\nBlackbird Interactive is seeking a passionate VFX Artist to join our team on an upcoming Third Person Action Shooter.\n\nDo you have a broad range of creative and technical experience building VFX in Unreal Engine 5? Are you skilled at creating art under a strong technical brief? If so, we’d love to hear from you!\n\nAt BBI, we’re a creative-fueled, future-driven, independent game studio where top talent can grow their careers while working on both world-class IPs and original creations across multiple genres. You’ll join a fast-moving team developing a Third Person Action Shooter.\n\nWe support remote and hybrid working arrangements across Canada (Vancouver, BC). At BBI, you’ll find a flexible, forward-thinking environment where creative voices are valued and nurtured.\n\nPlease include a link to your showreel with your Resume.\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n• Create and develop real-time VFX using Unreal Engine 5 and Niagara\n• Work with the Creative Leads to author immersive VFX for an FPS game\n• Problem-solve and support tools and tech development to achieve visual and performance targets in engine\n• Monitor deliverable progress, manage assigned scope and requested changes, and follow through on commitments\n• Ensure FX assets meet technical requirements for Unreal Engine 5\n• Work independently with minimal supervision, while collaborating effectively within the team and taking ownership of problems\n• Document tools and production pipelines in a clear and understandable way\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n• 2+ years of proven gameplay development experience\n• Demonstrated ability to work on multidisciplinary project teams and adapt to changing priorities throughout the product life cycle\n• Excellent communication and presentation skills\n• Experience with Unreal Engine 5 and Niagara\n• Experience with dynamic FX scaling and variable integration at runtime\n\nPLUSES\n• Unreal Blueprint Experience\n• Unreal chaos destruction experience",
