    "desc": "We are looking for a Senior Producer to join an exciting new project early in its development phases. You will get a chance to help build a multi-disciplinary team from the ground up, participate in hiring, establish how the team achieves success and then lead them towards those successes.\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n• Overseeing the development process, managing timelines, resources, scope, and quality\n• You are responsible for end-to-end delivery, ensuring predictable project outcomes through effective tracking, risk mitigation, and problem-solving\n• You understand pipelines, identify bottlenecks, and work systematically to improve efficiencies\n• Assume accountability for overall team progress and timely delivery of milestones and other key deliverables.\n• Ensure that needed ceremonies (such as stand-up, retros, progress reporting etc) are instituted and conducted.\n• Be a champion for your team by removing blockers, optimizing the flow of communication, facilitating collaboration and nurturing a sense of shared ownership.\n• Establish and continuously evolve workflows and pipelines.\n• Participate in hiring for your team and facilitate relaxed but efficient onboarding experiences.\n• Identify ways to leverage outsourcing opportunities where sensible\n• Assume people management responsibilities for a group of developers, supporting them in their growth and career development. You are accountable for the entire employee journey of your direct reports, from hiring to onboarding, probation period evaluation, all the way to eventual offboarding\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n• At least 5 years experience as a Producer or Project Manager.\n• Been involved with at least one game project through a complete development cycle.\n• Has led a full or significant part of a multi-disciplinary development team.\n• Thorough understanding of agile game development methodologies.\n• Experience of common tools of trade such as JIRA, Confluence, Figma etc.\n• Attention to detail and strong organizational skills.\n• Strong verbal and written communication skills in English.\n• Servant-leadership, team-first and collaborative mindset.\nNote: Research shows under-represented groups in the industry might not apply to a job if they don’t check off every requirement. At Avalanche, we’re more about your drive to learn and interest in tackling challenges than what’s on your resume! So don’t stress if you don’t tick every box— shoot us your application anyway! Diverse opinions and different experiences are what make our teams so great, not itemized lists of qualifications.\n\nThe Stockholm location\n\nOur Stockholm office is situated in Södermalm, the beating heart of the city’s game industry. It’s a physical representation of our games – the lush vegetation of Just Cause and theHunter: Call of the Wild meets corroded metal straight out of Mad Max. Our hybrid model requires you to be in the office on Mondays, Tuesdays, and Thursdays to foster collaboration and creativity.\n\nOur values\n\nAt Avalanche Studios Group, we create worlds beyond limits. But that’s not exclusive to our games, so we’re committed to developing a diverse and inclusive workplace. All Avalanchers have a shared responsibility to create an open work environment where everyone is treated equally and respectfully. Being part of our world is not contingent on your heritage, your gender, or sexual orientation. It’s all about your passion and creativity.\n\nHow to apply\n\nTo apply for this position, please register below and provide your CV in English. We review applications continuously. All further studio-related information is provided under a non-disclosure agreement.\n\nAt Avalanche Studios Group we're always on the lookout for talented individuals to join our passionate team, but please note that relocation assistance is not available for this role.",
